2536.23,2538.3,2529.4,2515.07,2510.64,2515.47,2509.5,2512.46,2513.11,2511.98],"sha256":"ad2c2beb24e194faf775dcf933936b2ae06505fc574ed2a8c3998975d79723c7","definition":"**Chosen definition (TradingView `ta.bb`):** mid[t] = SMA of the last n closes; sd[t] = POPULATION standard deviation of those n closes (divide by n, not n-1); upper = mid + mult*sd; lower = mid - mult*sd. Defaults n=20, mult=2 (SOURCED: standard Bollinger setting, TradingView default). `None` until n closes exist. Sample sd (n-1) is the known variant: it widens the band by sqrt(n/(n-1)) (2.6% at n=20) and is NOT used.\n\n**Worked example (n=4, mult=2, 6 bars):** closes = [8, 10, 10, 12, 14, 12]. Last window (idx 2..5) = [10, 12, 14, 12]: mean 12; deviations -2, 0, 2, 0; squares sum 8; population variance 8/4 = 2, sd = 1.414214; upper = 12 + 2.828427 = 14.828427, lower = 9.171573. (Sample sd would give sqrt(8/3) = 1.632993, upper 15.265986: the variant, not used.) First window (idx 0..3) = [8,10,10,12]: mean 10, squares 4+0+0+4 = 8, sd 1.414214, upper 12.828427, lower 7.171573.","question":"Compute Bollinger Bands with n=20 and mult=2 at the LAST close of the list: BB_mid, BB_up, BB_low.","answer_keys":["BB_mid","BB_up","BB_low"],"reply_format":"JSON object with exactly the answer_keys as keys and plain numbers as values, e.g. {\"BB_mid\": 0.0}"}